{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"A Short Tale of Janaka: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja52'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 52 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Āsīsavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Hope </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>2. Cūḷajanakajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A Short Tale of Janaka: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Vāyametheva puriso, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A man should make an effort </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na nibbindeyya paṇḍito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the astute should not be disillusioned. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Passāmi vohaṁ attānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Now I truly see myself, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>udakā thalamubbhatan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>lifted from the water to the shore. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Cūḷajanakajātakaṁ dutiyaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
